\[
(1 + i)^{13} = ( \sqrt{2} e^{i\pi/4} )^{13} = 2^{13/2} e^{i13\pi/4} = 64\sqrt{2} e^{i\pi/4}
\]
Simplifying, we get:
\[
(1 + i)^{13} = 64(1 + i)
\]

Similarly, for \(b = 1 - i\), we compute:
\[
(1 - i)^{13} = ( \sqrt{2} e^{-i\pi/4} )^{13} = 2^{13/2} e^{-i13\pi/4} = 64\sqrt{2} e^{-i\pi/4}
\]
Simplifying, we get:
\[
(1 - i)^{13} = 64(1 - i)
\]

Thus, we have:
\[
(1 + i)^{13} - 1 = 64(1 + i) - 1 = 63 + 64i
\]
\[
(1 - i)^{13} - 1 = 64(1 - i) - 1 = 63 - 64i
\]

Multiplying these results:
\[
(63 + 64i)(63 - 64i) = 63^2 + 64^2 = 3969 + 4096 = 8065
\]

Finally, we find the remainder when 8065 is divided by 1000:
\[
8065 \mod 1000 = 65
\]

